A class should have only 
      one reason to change, 
      meaning it should handle one responsibility only

Bad Example
        class User:
          def __init__(self, name):
              self.name = name
      
          def save_to_db(self):
              print("Saving user to database")
      
          def send_email(self):
              print("Sending email")

Good Example
        class User:
            def __init__(self, name):
                self.name = name
        
        
        class UserRepository:
            def save(self, user):
                print("Saving user to database")
        
        
        class EmailService:
            def send(self, user):
                print("Sending email")
